 2. 💰 Dems post &quot;mind-blowing&quot; numbers 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: FEC, Axios research. Chart: Noah Bressner/Axios This chart shows Democrats' staggering third-quarter fundraising advantage in nine closely watched Senate races — outraising Republicans in every one by at least $9 million.

 Why it matters: If money is momentum, Democratic Senate candidates are poised for a monumental Election Day, Axios' Hans Nichols writes. Republicans are awash in super PAC cash, but Democrats' advantage in hard dollars reveals a yawning enthusiasm gap — the kind of energy money can't buy.

 "Oh, my God! Holy crap," Sen. Bernie Moreno (R-Ohio) said when informed of Texas Democratic Senate nominee James Talarico's $64 million haul . "I mean, that's a number that's mind-blowing." Between the lines: The figures reflect FEC filings and campaign-reported totals, some of which include money raised through joint fundraising committees. 

