 3. ⚠️ The debt-fueled AI boom is cracking 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Allie Carl/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Wall Street appears to be hitting its limit on AI — and financiers are starting to say the quiet part out loud: All of this AI spending doesn't look like it can pay off for everyone, Axios' Madison Mills writes. 

 Why it matters: A massive gap is opening up between AI infrastructure spending and expected returns. AI providers are projected to spend $7 trillion on infrastructure through 2030. They're expected to generate no more than $3.6 trillion in related revenue over that same period, according to the Gartner consulting firm.

 Gartner also predicts that more than 80% of specialized AI cloud providers will cease operating independently by 2030. Explore the data ... Share this story . 

 
 
