 8. ⚾ 1 fun thing: Brew Crew dethrones Dodgers 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 L.A. Dodgers third baseman Kiké Hernández leaves the field after making the final out as the Milwaukee Brewers celebrate at Dodger Stadium last night. Photo: Mark J. Terrill/AP The Milwaukee Brewers are headed for their first World Series appearance since 1982 after completing a shocking sweep of the two-time defending champion Los Angeles Dodgers last night.

 Milwaukee — a small-market franchise that's never won a title — toppled baseball's highest-paid team and the sport's biggest star, Shohei Ohtani. The Brewers will face the winner of the American League Championship Series, where the Cleveland Guardians lead the Tampa Bay Rays, 2-1.

